/// Run On-Policy Distillation training on the provided prompts.
///
/// This implements the §3.1 pseudocode from the grand plan:
///
/// ```text
/// # Initialize teacher client (LogitSource).
/// # Sample trajectories (do_group_rollout on the student).
/// # Compute reward (per-token reverse KL via the OPD-loss kernel).
/// # Train with RL (importance-sampling loss; advantage = -reverse_kl).
/// ```
///
/// The mathematical guarantee from Lu (2025) is that this is "literally
/// one line on top of the GRPO trainer" — swap `reward - baseline` for
/// `-reverse_kl_per_token`. That observation is what makes this module
/// a sibling of `trainer.rs::grpo_train` rather than a fork.
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `prompts` — Prompts to train on. If empty, `dataset_path` must be set.
/// * `config` — Training configuration (§3.1 + §6 defaults).
/// * `model_config` — Model architecture config.
/// * `weights` — Loaded model weights (LoRA detached).
/// * `tokenizer` — Tokenizer for chat-template rendering.
/// * `adapter_dir` — Output directory for the trained adapter.
/// * `adapter_name` — Name for the output adapter.
/// * `teacher` — Teacher `LogitSource` for top-K logprobs.
/// * `progress_cb` — Progress callback for the dashboard.
/// * `replay_ctx` — Replay context for hot-swap + lineage tracking.
///
